One concrete overhead is per-call weight conversion: leaderboard timing regenerates weights every run, so transposed FP16 weights cannot be reused across timed samples. I’m checking the existing “raw weight” output kernel to see if avoiding the final weight transpose is worth any runtime without changing math.
